{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"e05380bdbc70e3e423e1fa9a70ac9bd3896e87857d3f4de0a1c2c274337365d8","digest":{"component_or_area":"push recovery (untracked-overwrite handling)","key_entities":["rebar._store.push_recovery._recover_dirty_merge","rebar._store.sync._untracked_overwrite_paths","rebar._store.sync._quarantine_dir_under","_merge_remote_under_lock","reconverge-quarantine","git reset --hard","git merge --abort","tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py","core._git"],"problem_keywords":["untracked-overwrite wedge","merge abort","push recovery","dirty merge","stash handling","colliding files","quarantine","recovery retry"],"propositions":["Push non-fast-forward recovery fails when an untracked local file collides with a file the merge wants to create, causing merge abort and repeated retry failures without self-healing.","The recovery path must quarantine colliding untracked files (matching sync.py reconverge behavior), retry the merge once, and restore the stash exactly once on all exit paths.","The shared untracked-overwrite parser from sync._untracked_overwrite_paths must be reused; quarantine moves happen through core._git late-binding, not sync's mover, to preserve push_recovery's test monkeypatch seam.","Genuine merge conflicts and unnamed paths retain today's behavior (abort, restore stash, warn/strict-raise); only untracked-overwrite collisions trigger quarantine-and-retry."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787892275146121001,"uuid":"093b0c50-ca59-4911-be36-e76fa595e302"}